Author: fwyc0573 <935953068@qq.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 1 14:46:27 2026 +0000

    kv-transfer: price grouped V4 NIXL wire time on physical blocks
    
    Native NIXL registers the packed V4 cache as one region with one
    block_stride descriptor per physical block, so each selected page of
    any cache group moves the full 1,002,240-byte block. The grouped path
    priced wire time on the structural component bytes (39,521,664 B for a
    6144-token prompt instead of the native 46,103,040 B per handle).
    
    Wire time now uses selected pages times physical_block_size_bytes.
    The recorded payload keeps its structural component bytes, so the
    ownership and end-event checks are unchanged. The grouped op trace
    records wire_bytes. Tests add the 256/257/6143 prompt boundaries and
    check the priced time against the wire bytes (D-WARM-TWO-FIX item 1).

